    "title": "Specter",
    "description": "Specter is a mobile app that allows users store and find digital geocaches to contextualize communication with location.\n\n-Implemented unit and end to end tests using KarmaJS and JasmineJS.\n-Developed a custom directive that converts geolocations into meaningful feedback that allows users   to discover digital geocaches.\n-Integrated ExpressJS backend with Ionic/Cordova front-end through Restangular service.\n-Reorganized the front end code using the latest Angular best practices.\n-Planned project sprints, created daily tasks and tracked completion of activities.\n\n",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2014 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "Plateful",
    "description": "Plateful is a mobile app for reviewing menu items in local restaurants.\n\n-Developed front-end with AngularJS ported to mobile with Ionic and Cordova.\n-Architected backend with ExpressJS, Mongoose and Neo4j database.\n-Integrated Google Places API, Yelp API and Foursquare API and combine the data to generate local restaurants’ information including menu, ratings, and reviews.\n-Utilized ngCordova to access the native camera, GPS, and microphone.\n",
